-- title:
--   Zariski-local injectivity of T⊗_S H¹(L_{S/R})→ H¹(L_{T/R})
-- statement:
--   Let $R$, $S$, $T$ be commutative rings with $S$ an $R$-algebra, $T$ an $R$-algebra and an $S$-algebra compatibly (a scalar tower $R \to S \to T$), and assume $T$ is flat as an $S$-module. Let $s$ be a subset of $T$ generating the unit ideal, $\mathrm{span}(s) = \top$. Assume that for every $g \in s$ there are an index type $\iota$ (in an arbitrary universe), a family $x : \iota \to T[1/g]$ of elements of the localization of $T$ away from $g$, and a finite list $f$ of polynomials in $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\iota\,S$ such that: the $S$-algebra map $\mathrm{aeval}\,x : S[X_i ; i \in \iota] \to T[1/g]$ is surjective; its kernel is the ideal generated by the entries of $f$; and for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $S[X_i ; i \in \iota]$ containing that ideal, the images of the entries of $f$, in the order given by the list, form a weakly regular sequence in the local ring $S[X_i ; i \in \iota]_{\mathfrak m}$. Then the $T$-linear map $T \otimes_S H^1(L_{S/R}) \to H^1(L_{T/R})$ obtained from `Algebra.H1Cotangent.map R R S T` by base change along $S \to T$ is injective.
--
--   This is the Zariski-local form of left exactness of the Jacobi–Zariski sequence for $R \to S \to T$ when $T$ is flat over $S$ and, locally on $T$, a relative complete intersection over $S$ in the weak sense that the defining equations are only required to be weakly regular in the local rings at the maximal ideals of the polynomial ring containing them. It is applied, via [`Algebra.H1Cotangent.liftBaseChange_map_injective_of_etale`](thm.html#Algebra.H1Cotangent.liftBaseChange_map_injective_of_etale), in the étale case, and its proof reduces the assertion to the one-chart statement [`Algebra.injective_liftBaseChange_h1CotangentMap_of_ker_eq_span_range_of_forall_exists_alternating`](thm.html#Algebra.injective_liftBaseChange_h1CotangentMap_of_ker_eq_span_range_of_forall_exists_alternating), where the relations are assumed to admit only alternating (Koszul) syzygies.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_injective_liftBaseChange_h1CotangentMap_of_span_eq_top_of_forall_exists_isWeaklyRegular.lean

